g.  All walkways were free and clear of debris.  Top of pits, vfd, doghouse were all clear of obstructions. ","location":"Clyde Barrow Unit 32-41 6 LS","service_line":"","report_number":"78925385","yard":""},{"date":"2026-04-09","observer":"Nicholas Sanchez","type":"At-Risk Condition, At-Risk Procedure","description":"Observed no barriers/ flagging around the catwalk. ","location":"Clyde Barrow Unit 32-41 6 LS","service_line":"","report_number":"78925233","yard":""}]},"near_misses":[{"date":"2026-04-09","observer":"Salvador Bazaldua","type":"Near Miss","description":"Shackle did not have a keeper in it","location":"H&p 266","service_line":"Casing","report_number":"78944393","yard":"Midland"}],"incidents":[{"date":"2026-04-09","employee":"","type":"Equipment Damage/Property Damage","description":"On this date, Steven Ortega and Germin Olivas were working at the Todd Micro Grid pad located northeast of the intersection of NM Hwy 128 and Red Road. Steven was operating a skid steer to move and dispense galvanized fence posts that were scheduled to be set later in the day. The crew was working in an area where a gate would eventually be erected.\n\nA third-party contractor had parked directly in front of the future gate location. A second truck approached and attempted to enter the work area but was unable to do so due to the first truck blocking access.\n\nObserving the situation, Steven began backing up the skid steer to allow the second truck to enter the work area through a gap between two posts that had not yet been connected. During this maneuver, Steven struck a post that supported the Emergency Shut-Off (ESO) switch for the facility. \n\nUpon realizing the incident, Steven immediately reported it and attempted to reposition the post. Shortly thereafter, another contractor arrived on-site and repaired both the post and the shut-off switch prior to the arrival of Butch's Safety personnel.\n\nFollowing the incident, the employee completed a post-accident drug and alcohol test on location, provided all required supporting documentation, and was subsequently released. In the hours following the incident, Safety personnel verified that both employees on-site had completed PEC SafeLand training. They also confirmed completion of the Devon Contractor Orientation, with supporting documentation attached.","location":"Todd Micro Grid","service_line":"Fencing","company":"Butch's Rat Hole & Anchor Service Inc","report_number":"78957344"}],"assessments":{"total":26,"details":[{"date":"2026-04-09","assessor":"Michael Salazar","form_id":381707,"form_name":"CSG - Safety Casing Field Assessment","division":"Casing","location":"","report_number":"78940533"},{"date":"2026-04-09","assessor":"James Barnett","form_id":381707,"form_name":"CSG - Safety Casing Field Assessment","division":"Casing","location":"","report_number":"78923203"},{"date":"2026-04-09","assessor":"Taurino Medrano","form_id":229645,"form_name":"CSG - Pre/Post Trip Inspection","division":"Casing","location":"","report_number":"78957712"},{"date":"2026-04-09","assessor":"James Sellers","form_id":229645,"form_name":"CSG - Pre/Post Trip Inspection","division":"Casing","location":"","report_number":"78957492"},{"date":"2026-04-09","assessor":"James Sellers","form_id":229645,"form_name":"CSG - Pre/Post Trip Inspection","division":"Casing","location":"","report_number":"78957413"},{"date":"2026-04-09","assessor":"Cesar Herrera Garcia","form_id":229645,"form_name":"CSG - Pre/Post Trip Inspection","division":"Casing","location":"","report_number":"78950609"},{"date":"2026-04-09","assessor":"Roger Gray","form_id":229645,"form_name":"CSG - Pre/Post Trip Inspection","division":"Casing","location":"","report_number":"78938011"},{"date":"2026-04-09","assessor":"Roger Gray","form_id":229645,"form_name":"CSG - Pre/Post Trip Inspection","division":"Casing","location":"","report_number":"78937761"},{"date":"2026-04-09","assessor":"Roger Gray","form_id":229645,"form_name":"CSG - Pre/Post Trip In